```

Wait: dirname may modify its argument; then basename on the same modified buffer → basename of the truncated string again! dirname("/a/b/c") truncates the buffer to "/a/b"… then basename(that) = "b". So we need two separate copies:

```c
	_cleanup_g_free_ gchar* namecopy1 = g_strdup(client->exportname);
	_cleanup_g_free_ gchar* namecopy2 = g_strdup(client->exportname);
	if (cowdir) dir = g_strdup(cowdir); else dir = g_strdup(dirname(namecopy1));
